id: pm-rlm-repair-runs
title: Repair only unsupported answer components within a fresh budget
description: "Evidence-directed repair resumes declared gaps while retaining valid supported components. Overlap check: host SDK provides certified reads, transactions, history, status roles and leases; pm-rlm evidence diagnoses gaps, adaptive plans initial work, reuse selects one complete call, reconciliation compares arms; pm-evidence manages citations and pm-rl evaluates policies. None schedules targeted repair of a partially supported answer."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T14:27:23.277Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T16:17:25.455Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One unsupported part among ten causes work only for that part and invalidated dependencies; budget exhaustion retains the supported answer with named gaps; no missing part is silently dropped. Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, strict schemas and remedies, no-git real public corpus validation, seeded state and interleaving evidence, npm and Bun CI gates."
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T14:28:00.396Z",codex-agent,"Design: explicit caller component DAG and source dependencies; native run per targeted component, fresh shared accounting, persistent revision-fenced repair controller, current SDK source revalidation before inference/retry, transitive skip propagation, original evidence retained with origin run references. No new import, export or sync command; journal interchange and native ledger round trips will be model-tested. Tests use only deterministic model adapters, real SDK trackers."
  "2026-10-27T14:51:10.363Z",codex-agent,"Public protocol-fixture validation passed on a verified read-only copy of unbraind/pm-lint at f2c20efa78139f4071f3dd08d317bea05337fe28: 12 source items, 54941 source JSON bytes, 30 unchanged read-only files. Ten components: one scheduled, nine reused, ten supported, one logical child, two model requests, 8181 charged tokens; resume adds zero requests. Zero budget retains nine supported answers and one named gap. Compact JSON is 2918 bytes. No external inference or runtime Git."
  "2026-10-27T15:02:24.481Z",codex-agent,"The behavioral revert proof passed in a disposable source copy: the zero-budget retention regression passes fixed code, fails when supported-component reuse is removed from the execution function, and passes after restoration (1/1). New state tests cover 500 seeded journal sequences, older inputs, native relationships and fields, random custom status roles/focus, source ABA changes, and competing executors at controller and SDK transaction transitions. Source reads now use public locateItem/readLocatedItem and runtime schema/type registry APIs rather than repeated full command projections."
  "2026-10-27T16:50:12.871Z",codex-agent,"Verified additional production boundaries: packed npm global and Bun global pm symlinks both pass (2/2). Three disposable behavioral reverts pass fixed, fail reverted, and pass restored: retained answers, history-fenced native checkpoint ABA rejection, and sparse evidence declarations (3/3). Native checkpoints now use the SDK item lock with the growing history length; controller operation identities use actual native history heads instead of serialized checkpoint counters. Read-only old snapshots remain available, and completion reloads durable state before metadata recovery."
  "2026-10-27T17:18:33.365Z",codex-agent,"The strengthened 500-sequence state model passed with 235 older-input replays over 12 real producer journals, recovering each through the package and comparing fresh SDK state. Typecheck, lint, docstrings (166 declarations) and zero-duplication checks pass. Public SDK declarations also confirm the newly used history-fenced mutation primitives exist at the declared 2026.10.18 host floor. Final review added pre-inference allowance/call-limit guards for late native children and accounting for a peer-completed child discovered after intent; focused regression and behavioral revert evidence remain in progress."
  "2026-10-27T17:52:52.505Z",codex-agent,"Final five behavioral reverts pass in a disposable copy: retained supported answers, native checkpoint ABA fencing, controller ABA fencing, late peer-child usage charged exactly once, and dense evidence declarations. Every case passes fixed code, fails the reverted behavior with an assertion, and passes after restoration (5/5). Typecheck, lint and the unchanged zero-duplication gate pass after consolidating SDK test read-back helpers."
  "2026-10-27T18:05:35.045Z",codex-agent,"Final accounting regression and its disposable revert pass (1/1), supplementing the previous five reverts. New repair children opt into the native engine verifier: stored totals must equal reconstructed charges, and settled reservations must equal recorded usage. Legacy native readers keep their policy. Fifteen initial-contract fault cases plus late peer completion pass (17/17); the final public measurement remains one scheduled, nine reused, ten supported, 8181 charged tokens, zero resume requests, and 2918 compact JSON bytes. The superseded local broad targeted run was stopped after about fifty minutes on the saturated host; its unfinished interleaving result is not approval. The final CI release gates will run the updated shared-tracker test, which retains native audit history while removing completed fixture rows between injections."
  "2026-10-27T18:10:58.824Z",codex-agent,"Final schema fuzz passes 1/1 and the public read-only measurement passes with unchanged numbers after strict accounting. Changelog generation/check pass. Strict tracker health passes with an isolated home and Git identity configuration, including extension, integrity, history and storage checks; the ambient home alone discovers a newer external extension and reports host-version skew, so that ambient result is not used as CI evidence. The agent claim is released and the item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. Full npm and Bun release evidence will be collected from the branch CI workflow before reporting readiness."
  "2026-10-27T18:46:17.921Z",codex-agent,"CI on f0df94b failed: the PR Node 26 suite reported 447/451 passing, with a killed primitive writer leaving an SDK item lock that command completion did not recover, two outdated behavioral-revert transforms, and the enclosing shallow-proof failure. Measured coverage was 100 statements/functions/lines and 99.1 overall branches, with repair branches 93.19. Follow-up uses the supported native lock policy before completion; the real root-write SIGKILL regression now passes 1/1. Both old revert transforms are updated for the history fence and captured read version. New source-chain, malformed-birth, child-integrity, publication/read/final-receipt and busy/transport regressions pass 5/5; the configured loopback HTTP model and source-contract checks pass 2/2. New SDK step boundaries are observable and included by the generated interleaving test. The committed pre-follow-up interleaving test passed all 33 transitions, and final-head npm/Bun global installs passed 2/2. Fresh full npm/Bun gates remain required; no green release-gate claim is made. Prior runs: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40557881142 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40557876926. The queue rules CI wait cutoff has been reached; the follow-up will request a fresh run and report it pending."
  "2026-10-27T20:12:01.336Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up integrity checks bind continued children to the producer question, model policy and allowance. Uncertain usage blocks new inference while preserving completed peers; a later resume reads native peer completion even after a saved gap. Foreign subcalls and unreachable native records are refused before materialization. Four additional disposable behavioral reverts each pass fixed, fail reverted with an assertion, and pass restored (4/4), supplementing six prior cases. Native ownership, graph and positive-budget older-journal smoke checks pass 3/3. The seeded 500-sequence model now includes four completed native children among twelve producer journals; the earlier zero-budget edition passed 500 sequences with 235 older replays, while this expanded edition and additional interleaving boundaries await fresh CI. Typecheck, lint, complete docstrings and unchanged zero-duplication checks pass. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/39 remains ready for review; the first CI result is failed (447/451), and fresh npm/Bun full gates will be requested after this commit and reported pending at the existing queue-rule cutoff. The item stays in_progress and this agent releases its claim."
  "2026-10-28T15:48:38.134Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1: resumed journal intent is not current execution authority. General rule: every new materialization and inference admission must check current remaining token and call headroom, even if an older intent recorded an allocation; exhaustion returns retained supported components with named gaps. Merged origin/main first, preserving its bounded dead-owner lock retry policy together with this branch history fences. Audit scope covers all prepareRlmRun callers (repair, adaptive, reconciliation, reuse, evaluation and native run), the shared SDK/CLI dispatch and JSON/TOON receipts, packed npm/Bun consumers and non-git trackers. Only one actionable review finding was supplied; GitHub exposes no additional inline/review findings. The existing item is reused, remains in_progress, and no completed validation is treated as fresh-head approval."
  "2026-10-28T15:58:54.700Z",codex-agent,"Class audit complete: repair is the only controller that resumes an unmaterialized child intent and derives its allocation from earlier children. Both new and saved intents now call the same current-headroom admission before native preparation; completed children bypass allocation and are verified normally. Adaptive decomposition reserves the native first-step floor for every future group and stops at exhausted call slots; reconciliation reserves each future floor and call slot inside disjoint arms. Native run, reuse and evaluation validate fresh configured settings and have no carried child allocation. CLI repair and repair-resume share the SDK implementation and compact producer; packed acceptance now reuses one installed-consumer fixture across npm/Bun global, project-local, npx/bunx and JSON/TOON. The reported crash reproduces before the fix. Focused lifecycle/retention and durable-completion checks pass 2/2, covering five phase/damage combinations. The disposable admission revert passes fixed, fails reverted with an assertion, and passes restored (1/1). Earlier CI on 90e7fae reported 460/463 and 99.96 branch coverage: main now supplies bounded dead-owner recovery; the stale completion proof is strengthened with assert.doesNotReject, and native empty/invalid history refusal coverage is added. No threshold or old assertion is weakened."
  "2026-10-28T16:16:40.354Z",codex-agent,"Final focused evidence for re-review: admission fixed/reverted/restored proof 1/1; strengthened durable-completion proof 1/1; bounded lock-retry behavioral reverts 4/4. Lifecycle plus completion checks pass 2/2; intact positive-budget saved-intent recovery passes 1/1 with exactly one child and zero extra inference on retry. Lock/deadline/history checks pass 12/12 including real SIGKILL recovery and empty/invalid controller history. Packed npm and Bun global hosts pass 2/2 with installed SDK and CLI JSON/TOON retention. The broader local legacy revert script timed out on cleanup after six observed assertions, and is not counted as approval; the entire unchanged shallow-proof gate remains required in CI. The two-worker limit was briefly exceeded by an extra focused run; that run was stopped, not counted, and its later rerun passed. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication (0/13775 lines), docstrings (36 source files, 159 declarations) and isolated strict tracker health pass. The existing project-local/npx/bunx packed suite remains in progress locally; final receipts and fresh exact-head npm/Bun release-gate URLs/counts will be maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/39. No SDK pin, gate threshold, old assertion or deadline was relaxed. The item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
